    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer dielectric multilayer filter on CaF2 substrate for dual-band infrared transmission. Layer sequence: Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS (24 finite layers, alternating Ge and ZnS starting with Ge). Wavelength bands: passbands at 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm (maximize transmittance), stopbands at 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm (minimize transmittance). Normal incidence, unpolarized light, coherent TMM. Initialize all Ge layers at 550 nm and all ZnS layers at 900 nm (quarter-wave at 4.4 μm center). Optimization bounds: Ge [400, 700] nm, ZnS [650, 1150] nm. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with learning rate 0.002, clamp thickness changes to ±15% of nominal values for first 3 epochs, then release full bounds. Maximum 500 optimization iterations. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 24-layer dielectric multilayer filter (Ge-ZnS alternating, starting with Ge) on a CaF2 substrate for dual-band infrared transmission between 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm, while suppressing transmittance in stopbands 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm under normal incidence unpolarized light using coherent TMM. Initialize Ge at 550 nm and ZnS at 900 nm, optimize within Ge [400, 700] nm and ZnS [650, 1150] nm bounds using Adam-LBFGS over 500 iterations.",
